EVALUATION.md §1, CODEGEN.md §5.9: gen/go's data loader refuses a map in a class it decodes, one an emitted value holds; Loose, held by no value, is not decoded and is fine.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A row.
record Row {
  /// The cells.
  cells: {String: Int}
}

/// Not held by any value.
record Loose {
  /// The cells.
  cells: {String: Int}
}

/// The rows.
let rows: table Row = {
  one { cells: {"a": 1} }
}

emit go { out: "@features/a", package: "a", mode: data }
emit json { out: "out/" }
-- a.rows.json --
{"one": {"cells": {"a": 1}}}
-- findings.txt --
error[E8019]  a/a.canon:6:3
  emit go in data mode cannot generate a map

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
